me materials as the roof: bricks, lime, and brick-dust. That which is realized intuitively as Brahman, through the eliminating process of ''Not this, not this'', is then found to have become the universe and all its living …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": null, "page_or_section": "Gospel vol. 1, ch. 3 (5 Aug 1882)", "relationship": "supports", "section_title": "Ramakrishna Paramahamsa: He distinguishes the jnani, who reaches Brahman by negating the world step by step, from the vijnani, who then finds that the steps are made of the same material as the roof — that Brahman has itself become the universe and living beings.", "source_id": "6bd19767-fd30-4b73-900b-11576daedd8e", "textual_layer": "Reported teachings: M.''s diary-style record of Ramakrishna''s conversations, in translation"}], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Mahendranath Gupta (M.), translated by Swami Nikhilananda", "authority_metadata": {"verified_at": "2026-10-12"}, "citation": "Mahendranath Gupta (M.), translated by Swami Nikhilananda. The Gospel of Sri Ramakrishna (Kathamrita): conversations recorded by M.. Ramakrishna-Vivekananda Center, New York (1942); online edition ramakrishnavivekananda.info. https://www.ramakrishnavivekananda.info/gospel/gospel.htm", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": 1942, "publisher_or_institution": "Ramakrishna-Vivekananda Center, New York (1942); online edition ramakrishnavivekananda.info", "rights_or_access_note": "Translation of the Bengali Kathamrita; Sil and others argue the translation omits or softens some passages.", "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "primary_text", "storage_path": null, "title": "The Gospel of Sri Ramakrishna (Kathamrita): conversations recorded by M.", "url": "https://www.ramakrishnavivekananda.info/gospel/gospel.htm"}, "source_id": "6bd19767-fd30-4b73-900b-11576daedd8e"}], "unmatched_passage_links": []}'::jsonb,'draft','ai_candidate');
