anda, and the Ranee of Jhansi. The high descent of the Ranee, her unbounded liberality to her troops and retainers, and her fortitude, which no reverses could …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": null, "page_or_section": "p. 1595", "relationship": "supports", "section_title": "Rani Lakshmibai of Jhansi: Hugh Rose''s dispatch on the capture of Calpee (Kalpi), 22 June 1858", "source_id": "a9c22a74-dd4f-4a15-b618-11ac985dfdc7", "textual_layer": "Contemporary British command report published in 1859; adversarial assessment"}], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Hugh Rose", "authority_metadata": {"verified_at": "2026-10-11"}, "citation": "Hugh Rose. Hugh Rose''s dispatch on the capture of Calpee (Kalpi), 22 June 1858. The London Gazette, 18 April 1859, p. 1595. https://www.thegazette.co.uk/London/issue/22251/page/1595/data.pdf", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": 1859, "publisher_or_institution": "The London Gazette, 18 April 1859, p. 1595", "rights_or_access_note": "Public original; short research excerpts. Scholarly abstract/summary access does not imply full chapter access.", "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "primary_text", "storage_path": null, "title": "Hugh Rose''s dispatch on the capture of Calpee (Kalpi), 22 June 1858", "url": "https://www.thegazette.co.uk/London/issue/22251/page/1595/data.pdf"}, "source_id": "a9c22a74-dd4f-4a15-b618-11ac985dfdc7"}], "unmatched_passage_links": []}'::jsonb,'draft','ai_candidate');
