to all of the gods. ''Let safety betide …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": "curated_source_token_overlap", "page_or_section": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful Majesties\n Sarga 60 in Prose", "relationship": "supports", "section_title": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful Majesties\n Sarga 60 in Prose", "source_id": "2ac81052-5bd0-4907-9e76-0deeaf0768d2", "textual_layer": "Ramayana — Bala Kanda"}, {"chunk_id": "6d6d9134-993a-496d-8286-852086790698", "confidence": 0.853333333333333, "excerpt": "\" ''Oh, ruler of people, now you shall see the potency of my ascesis which I personally  achieved. Such as I am I shall lead you forth to haven with your own body just by  my personal capability. Oh, king of people, now you will go to heaven with your  own mortal body, which is otherwise unattainable. May it be a little, but there  is some fruit of my …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": "curated_source_token_overlap", "page_or_section": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful Majesties\n Sarga 60 in Prose", "relationship": "supports", "section_title": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful Majesties\n Sarga 60 in Prose", "source_id": "2ac81052-5bd0-4907-9e76-0deeaf0768d2", "textual_layer": "Ramayana — Bala Kanda"}], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Valmiki", "authority_metadata": {}, "citation": "Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda, Sarga 60 (https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga60/bala_60_prose.htm)", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "Valmiki Ramayana project", "rights_or_access_note": null, "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "scholarly_article", "storage_path": null, "title": "Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda, Sarga 60", "url": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga60/bala_60_prose.htm"}, "source_id": "2ac81052-5bd0-4907-9e76-0deeaf0768d2"}], "unmatched_passage_links": []}'::jsonb,'approved','system_test_bulk');
insert into original_claims values ('4a592c1a-e288-4336-b47b-de9d0afe6031','{"approval_origin": "system_test_bulk", "certainty": "high", "claim_id": "4a592c1a-e288-4336-b47b-de9d0afe6031", "claim_kind": "traditional_account", "claim_relations": [], "claim_text": "The Mahabharata Sarasvati curse story encodes sacred geography and rivalry through supernatural causation; it can document the epic''s tirtha tradition without being presented as literal river history.", "current_status": "approved", "epistemics": {"contract_basis": null, "contract_satisfied": false, "contract_status": "NEEDS_TYPE_REVIEW", "epistemic_type": null, "proposed_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "reviewer_kind": null, "type_origin": "deterministic", "type_review_status": "needs_type_review"}, "evidence_flags": ["No active supporting passage linked to an approved source", "Missing assigned epistemic classification", "Current approval origin does not establish strict verification", "Retention/access rights note missing for an associated source", "Recorded source access issue"], "evidence_type": "traditional_narrative", "lens": {"field_id": "8d36194b-360a-499b-a5a1-e055ce8db12b", "field_label": "Mythologization vs. historical core, explicitly flagged rather than artificially resolved", "parameter_id": "e9e12cd4-53da-4743-8917-a2868006ced2", "parameter_name": "Contested or Uncertain Aspects"}, "parent_claim_id": null, "personality_id": "2853f4ed-98b1-4ef8-9f30-30f85d42edad", "personality_name": "Vishvamitra", "reviewer_decision": null, "sources": [{"evidence_excerpt": "The Shalya Parva narrative explains blood-mixed river water through Vishvamitra''s curse.", "link_id": "b13d2fef-ab3a-4811-bc95-a0111e3327ca", "page_or_section": "Vasisthapavaha", "passages": [], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Vyasa (traditional attribution); BORI Critical Edition", "authority_metadata": {}, "citation": "Mahabharata BORI, Shalya Parva", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "Bhandarkar Oriental Research Institute critical text / Vedapath presentation", "rights_or_access_note": null, "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "scholarly_article", "storage_path": null, "title": "Mahabharata (BORI Critical Edition), Shalya Parva", "url": "https://vedapath.app/en/mahabharata-bori/shalya-parva"}, "source_id": "1235fefa-2528-496e-86d5-4297dbe57f04"}], "unmatched_passage_links": []}'::jsonb,'approved','system_test_bulk');
insert into original_claims values ('4d7839f8-7966-4f4c-b6f0-7c22a3771c2f','{"approval_origin": "system_test_bulk", "certainty": "high", "claim_id": "4d7839f8-7966-4f4c-b6f0-7c22a3771c2f", "claim_kind": "traditional_account", "claim_relations": [], "claim_text": "The smoke-and-world-burning imagery at the climax of Vishvamitra''s tapas should be classified as epic supernatural narration, even though the narrative uses it to mark the extremity of his ascetic power.", "current_status": "approved", "epistemics": {"contract_basis": null, "contract_satisfied": false, "contract_status": "NEEDS_TYPE_REVIEW", "epistemic_type": null, "proposed_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "reviewer_kind": null, "type_origin": "deterministic", "type_review_status": "needs_type_review"}, "evidence_flags": ["No active supporting passage linked to an approved source", "Missing assigned epistemic classification", "Current approval origin does not establish strict verification", "Recorded source access issue", "Claim-passage link points to a source absent from claim-source links"], "evidence_type": "traditional_narrative", "lens": {"field_id": "8d36194b-360a-499b-a5a1-e055ce8db12b", "field_label": "Mythologization vs. historical core, explicitly flagged rather than artificially resolved", "parameter_id": "e9e12cd4-53da-4743-8917-a2868006ced2", "parameter_name": "Contested or Uncertain Aspects"}, "parent_claim_id": null, "personality_id": "2853f4ed-98b1-4ef8-9f30-30f85d42edad", "personality_name": "Vishvamitra", "reviewer_decision": null, "sources": [{"evidence_excerpt": "The worlds are described as distressed by heat as smoke issues from his head.", "link_id": "85f96edb-9d8b-4658-bf87-99121aa79f17", "page_or_section": "1.65", "passages": [], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Valmiki (traditional attribution)", "authority_metadata": {}, "citation": "Valmiki Ramayana", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "IIT Kanpur Valmiki Ramayanam Project", "rights_or_access_note": "The original IITK link has a TLS certificate mismatch. A readable parallel translation of the same Bala Kanda chapter is linked below; compare editions before using a quotation.", "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "primary_text", "storage_path": null, "title": "Valmiki Ramayanam, Bala Kanda, Sarga 65", "url": "https://www.valmiki.iitk.ac.in/summary?field_kanda_tid=1&field_sarga_value=65"}, "source_id": "35d30c22-48b6-4242-ad17-697405136d76"}], "unmatched_passage_links": [{"chunk_id": "78708c3d-c722-4223-95c2-92c74a53f606", "excerpt": "\" ''All the beings in the triad of the worlds are very highly perturbed at their  senses and they are as though stupefied, and when juxtaposed the sun is lustreless  before the resplendence of that great sage. [1-65-15b, 16a]  बुद्धिम् न कुरुते यावत् नाशे देव महामुनिः || १-६५-१६ तावत् प्रसादो भगवान् अग्नि रूपो महाद्युतिः |  16b, 17a. deva = oh, god; …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "page_or_section": "Introduction", "relationship": "context", "source": {"author": "Valmiki", "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "Valmiki Ramayana project", "rights_or_access_note": null, "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "scholarly_article", "title": "Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda, Sarga 65", "url": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga65/balasans65.htm.orig"}, "source_id": "b1ff445c-d9d0-4f8e-a28f-f3a8053787ad"}, {"chunk_id": "ef5de7fd-af8f-4eaa-9685-ac9b0a43aa7d", "excerpt": "Vishvamitra becomes Brahma-sage after a prolonged ascesis that made all the worlds  to startle. All gods request Brahma to accord the supreme Brahma-sageship on Vishvamitra  as he is cleansed of all mortal impurities, and Brahma accords that highest order  on him. Thus Sage Shataananda concludes his narration about the legend of Vishvamitra.  अथ हैमवतीम् …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "page_or_section": "Introduction", "relationship": "context", "source": {"author": "Valmiki", "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "Valmiki Ramayana project", "rights_or_access_note": null, "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "scholarly_article", "title": "Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda, Sarga 65", "url": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga65/balasans65.htm.orig"}, "source_id": "b1ff445c-d9d0-4f8e-a28f-f3a8053787ad"}]}'::jsonb,'approved','system_test_bulk');
insert into original_claims values ('59b3af71-7c8d-4511-a8ba-753629e90399','{"approval_origin": "system_test_bulk", "certainty": "high", "claim_id": "59b3af71-7c8d-4511-a8ba-753629e90399", "claim_kind": "traditional_account", "claim_relations": [], "claim_text": "Cross-source agreement on a broad motif—Vishvamitra''s association with kingship, tapas, and brahmanic status—does not by itself prove that all detailed Vedic, Brahmana, Ramayana, and Mahabharata episodes belong to one historical biography.", "current_status": "approved", "epistemics": {"contract_basis": null, "contract_satisfied": false, "contract_status": "NEEDS_TYPE_REVIEW", "epistemic_type": null, "proposed_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "reviewer_kind": null, "type_origin": "deterministic", "type_review_status": "needs_type_review"}, "evidence_flags": ["No active supporting passage linked to an approved source", "Missing assigned epistemic classification", "Current approval origin does not establish strict verification", "Retention/access rights note missing for an associated source"], "evidence_type": "traditional_narrative", "lens": {"field_id": "8d36194b-360a-499b-a5a1-e055ce8db12b", "field_label": "Mythologization vs. historical core, explicitly flagged rather than artificially resolved", "parameter_id": "e9e12cd4-53da-4743-8917-a2868006ced2", "parameter_name": "Contested or Uncertain Aspects"}, "parent_claim_id": null, "personality_id": "2853f4ed-98b1-4ef8-9f30-30f85d42edad", "personality_name": "Vishvamitra", "reviewer_decision": null, "sources": [{"evidence_excerpt": "The corpus contains related motifs across independent textual layers with substantial differences in detail.", "link_id": "e03d5200-532b-4e61-a0e4-53e3a8f5214e", "page_or_section": "Historical-method caution", "passages": [], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Mahidasa Aitareya (traditional attribution)", "authority_metadata": {}, "citation": "Aitareya Brahmana", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "Vedic Heritage Portal / IGNCA / Ministry of Culture, Government of India", "rights_or_access_note": null, "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "institutional", "storage_path": null, "title": "Aitareya Brahmana", "url": "https://vedicheritage.gov.in/brahmanas/aitareya-brahmana/"}, "source_id": "d7d8aaa4-5733-44cf-b9bf-0f494d707b99"}], "unmatched_passage_links": []}'::jsonb,'approved','system_test_bulk');
insert into original_claims values ('68d6c632-9f87-4185-a79d-5ca204aac047','{"approval_origin": "system_test_bulk", "certainty": "high", "claim_id": "68d6c632-9f87-4185-a79d-5ca204aac047", "claim_kind": "traditional_account", "claim_relations": [], "claim_text": "The episode in which celestial weapons appear as speaking beings after mantra transmission is securely part of the Ramayana narrative but is not independent evidence that weapons literally took anthropomorphic form.", "current_status": "approved", "epistemics": {"contract_basis": null, "contract_satisfied": false, "contract_status": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "epistemic_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "proposed_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "reviewer_kind": null, "type_origin": "deterministic", "type_review_status": "auto_assigned"}, "evidence_flags": ["No active supporting passage linked to an approved source", "Current approval origin does not establish strict verification", "Recorded source access issue"], "evidence_type": "traditional_narrative", "lens": {"field_id": "8d36194b-360a-499b-a5a1-e055ce8db12b", "field_label": "Mythologization vs. historical core, explicitly flagged rather than artificially resolved", "parameter_id": "e9e12cd4-53da-4743-8917-a2868006ced2", "parameter_name": "Contested or Uncertain Aspects"}, "parent_claim_id": null, "personality_id": "2853f4ed-98b1-4ef8-9f30-30f85d42edad", "personality_name": "Vishvamitra", "reviewer_decision": null, "sources": [{"evidence_excerpt": "Verses 1.27.23-24 personify the astras and have them address Rama.", "link_id": "efddadcc-fe3e-44bb-97a7-ce9ca0aaf55c", "page_or_section": "1.27.23-24", "passages": [{"chunk_id": "4cd2f9db-d7f3-4cbf-a7ba-5ba1b92b5363", "confidence": 0.55, "excerpt": "\"Oh, mighty armed son of the best king, I am giving a great missile named Vaidyadhara  by its name, and a gem of sword named Nandana. Thus, the missile which is very much liked by Gandharva-s,  namely Mohana, [The Stupefier,] the missile called Prasvapana [The Inducer of Sleep,] and the gentle  Prashamana, [The Pacifier of enemy''s anger.]  \"Oh, highly …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": "citation_partial", "page_or_section": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful MajestiesSarga 27 in Prose", "relationship": "context", "section_title": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful MajestiesSarga 27 in Prose", "source_id": "810e23ca-7c61-499e-85f4-e37468b88b6f", "textual_layer": "Ramayana — Bala Kanda"}, {"chunk_id": "d76099f9-326d-4287-88a0-b53e1c0a17a8", "confidence": 0.78, "excerpt": "The nature of some astra-s - missiles  There are some verses that depict the nature of these astra-s. A few of them are  given under. Though we may not actually acquire a projectile power with these verses, they may at least  detail what these missiles are. The source of these verses is untraceable, but they are said to be in  puraaNaa-s, and Shiva informs …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": "adaptive_strong", "page_or_section": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful MajestiesSarga 27 in Prose", "relationship": "context", "section_title": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful MajestiesSarga 27 in Prose", "source_id": "810e23ca-7c61-499e-85f4-e37468b88b6f", "textual_layer": "Ramayana — Bala Kanda"}], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Valmiki (traditional attribution); English rendering by Desiraju Hanumanta Rao", "authority_metadata": {"verified_http_status": 200}, "citation": "Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda 1.27, chapter-level prose rendering.", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "Valmiki Ramayana project", "rights_or_access_note": "Publicly accessible chapter page; preserve source attribution and link.", "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "primary_text", "storage_path": null, "title": "Valmiki Ramayana — Bala Kanda, Sarga 27 (prose)", "url": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga27/bala_27_prose.htm"}, "source_id": "810e23ca-7c61-499e-85f4-e37468b88b6f"}, {"evidence_excerpt": "Verses 1.27.23-24 personify the astras and have them address Rama.", "link_id": "e1b1d6c6-cb22-44ed-b180-de206bbf92b7", "page_or_section": "1.27.23-24", "passages": [], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Valmiki (traditional attribution)", "authority_metadata": {}, "citation": "Valmiki Ramayana", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "IIT Kanpur Valmiki Ramayanam Project", "rights_or_access_note": "The original IITK link has a TLS certificate mismatch. A readable parallel translation of the same Bala Kanda chapter is linked below; compare editions before using a quotation.", "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "primary_text", "storage_path": null, "title": "Valmiki Ramayanam, Bala Kanda, Sarga 27", "url": "https://www.valmiki.iitk.ac.in/sloka?field_kanda_tid=1&field_sarga_value=27&language=dv"}, "source_id": "f1d7e0f2-22cc-4086-84d5-66fb03fdef01"}], "unmatched_passage_links": []}'::jsonb,'approved','system_test_bulk');
insert into original_claims values ('70927283-3b37-4ce6-b345-a6180f4d0896','{"approval_origin": "system_test_bulk", "certainty": "high", "claim_id": "70927283-3b37-4ce6-b345-a6180f4d0896", "claim_kind": "traditional_account", "claim_relations": [], "claim_text": "Mahabharata Anushasana Parva''s charu-exchange birth story is a tradition-specific explanation of Vishvamitra''s mixed royal and brahmanic identity and should not be treated as biomedical or historical mechanism.", "current_status": "approved", "epistemics": {"contract_basis": null, "contract_satisfied": false, "contract_status": "NEEDS_TYPE_REVIEW", "epistemic_type": null, "proposed_type": "METHODOLOGICAL", "reviewer_kind": null, "type_origin": "deterministic", "type_review_status": "needs_type_review"}, "evidence_flags": ["No active supporting passage linked to an approved source", "Missing assigned epistemic classification", "Current approval origin does not establish strict verification", "Retention/access rights note missing for an associated source", "Recorded source access issue"], "evidence_type": "traditional_narrative", "lens": {"field_id": "8d36194b-360a-499b-a5a1-e055ce8db12b", "field_label": "Mythologization vs. historical core, explicitly flagged rather than artificially resolved", "parameter_id": "e9e12cd4-53da-4743-8917-a2868006ced2", "parameter_name": "Contested or Uncertain Aspects"}, "parent_claim_id": null, "personality_id": "2853f4ed-98b1-4ef8-9f30-30f85d42edad", "personality_name": "Vishvamitra", "reviewer_decision": null, "sources": [{"evidence_excerpt": "The chapter attributes character and lineage outcomes to mantra-prepared ritual food and exchanged rites.", "link_id": "b547adb5-018a-4394-b305-47c3988a5cd9", "page_or_section": "13.4", "passages": [], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Vyasa (traditional attribution); BORI Critical Edition", "authority_metadata": {}, "citation": "Mahabharata BORI, Anushasana Parva, 4", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year":