silence while the princes perform protective duty.", "link_id": "b68af461-8db5-473d-b897-c5f2b1ec69a6", "page_or_section": "1.30", "passages": [], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Valmiki (traditional attribution)", "authority_metadata": {}, "citation": "Valmiki Ramayana", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "IIT Kanpur Valmiki Ramayanam Project", "rights_or_access_note": "The original IITK link has a TLS certificate mismatch. A readable parallel translation of the same Bala Kanda chapter is linked below; compare editions before using a quotation.", "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "primary_text", "storage_path": null, "title": "Valmiki Ramayanam, Bala Kanda, Sarga 30", "url": "https://www.valmiki.iitk.ac.in/summary?field_kanda_tid=1&field_sarga_value=30"}, "source_id": "c006a140-843f-4e0f-bd26-d6f273aeb801"}], "unmatched_passage_links": []}'::jsonb,'approved','system_test_bulk');
insert into original_claims values ('5c0d6459-cb4f-4fe4-b012-8b62d4972b43','{"approval_origin": "system_test_bulk", "certainty": "high", "claim_id": "5c0d6459-cb4f-4fe4-b012-8b62d4972b43", "claim_kind": "textual_tradition", "claim_relations": [], "claim_text": "Vishvamitra is the catalyst who takes Rama and Lakshmana from Ayodhya into the sequence of events that dominates early Bala Kanda.", "current_status": "approved", "epistemics": {"contract_basis": "tradition", "contract_satisfied": true, "contract_status": "SUPPORTED", "epistemic_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "proposed_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "reviewer_kind": null, "type_origin": "deterministic", "type_review_status": "auto_assigned"}, "evidence_flags": ["Current approval origin does not establish strict verification", "Retention/access rights note missing for an associated source"], "evidence_type": "traditional_narrative", "lens": {"field_id": "480af3d9-6cea-428a-8b51-7a4c721f8545", "field_label": "Role in Ramayana / Mahabharata narratives when applicable", "parameter_id": "700ce11a-bd45-4116-99a4-a246dc97c505", "parameter_name": "Relational / Social Role"}, "parent_claim_id": null, "personality_id": "2853f4ed-98b1-4ef8-9f30-30f85d42edad", "personality_name": "Vishvamitra", "reviewer_decision": null, "sources": [{"evidence_excerpt": "His request to Dasharatha initiates Rama''s departure to protect the sacrifice.", "link_id": "a01f60b3-e070-4546-85a0-33feec639d53", "page_or_section": "1.19", "passages": [{"chunk_id": "405d9d7b-f196-44bf-b8db-e65a2e9886f2", "confidence": 0.8575, "excerpt": "न च तौ राममासाद्य शक्तौ स्थातुं कथञ्चन || १-१९-११  न च तौ राघवादन्यो हन्तुमुत्सहते पुमान् |  11b, 12a. tau = those two [demons]; raamam aasaadya = on getting [affronting] Rama   ; katha~nchana = in any way; sthaatum   = to stand fast; na shaktau = not, capable; raaghavaat anyaH pumaan   = other person than Raghava; tau hantum na utsahate = do not have …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": "curated_source_token_overlap", "page_or_section": "Introduction", "relationship": "supports", "section_title": "Introduction", "source_id": "826d5c8a-6135-4304-8825-09579ff9a478", "textual_layer": "Ramayana — Bala Kanda, Sarga 19"}, {"chunk_id": "9374da7d-e000-40d3-83fc-7d752aa7f76c", "confidence": 0.89, "excerpt": "Sage Vishvamitra asks King Dasharatha to send Rama to protect the Vedic ritual   that is being conducted by him, from the demons that are constantly disrupting   it. The sage asserts King Dasharatha that he and the other sages in Dasharatha''s   court know the capabilities of Rama and though Rama is in his adolescence, he   can easily kill the demons. But …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": "curated_source_token_overlap", "page_or_section": "Introduction", "relationship": "supports", "section_title": "Introduction", "source_id": "826d5c8a-6135-4304-8825-09579ff9a478", "textual_layer": "Ramayana — Bala Kanda, Sarga 19"}], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Valmiki", "authority_metadata": {}, "citation": "Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda, Sarga 19 (https://valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga19/balasans19.htm)", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "Valmiki Ramayana project", "rights_or_access_note": null, "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "scholarly_article", "storage_path": null, "title": "Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda, Sarga 19", "url": "https://valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga19/balasans19.htm"}, "source_id": "826d5c8a-6135-4304-8825-09579ff9a478"}], "unmatched_passage_links": []}'::jsonb,'approved','system_test_bulk');
insert into original_claims values ('70f6b183-1ca5-4f8b-87bb-2db1836e80d6','{"approval_origin": "system_test_bulk", "certainty": "high", "claim_id": "70f6b183-1ca5-4f8b-87bb-2db1836e80d6", "claim_kind": "textual_tradition", "claim_relations": [], "claim_text": "He is also the narrator through whom Rama hears the Kusa dynasty tradition, expanding his role from combat mentor into transmitter of royal genealogy.", "current_status": "approved", "epistemics": {"contract_basis": "tradition", "contract_satisfied": true, "contract_status": "SUPPORTED", "epistemic_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "proposed_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "reviewer_kind": null, "type_origin": "deterministic", "type_review_status": "auto_assigned"}, "evidence_flags": ["Current approval origin does not establish strict verification", "Recorded source access issue"], "evidence_type": "traditional_narrative", "lens": {"field_id": "480af3d9-6cea-428a-8b51-7a4c721f8545", "field_label": "Role in Ramayana / Mahabharata narratives when applicable", "parameter_id": "700ce11a-bd45-4116-99a4-a246dc97c505", "parameter_name": "Relational / Social Role"}, "parent_claim_id": null, "personality_id": "2853f4ed-98b1-4ef8-9f30-30f85d42edad", "personality_name": "Vishvamitra", "reviewer_decision": null, "sources": [{"evidence_excerpt": "Sarga 32 contains Vishvamitra''s dynastic account.", "link_id": "552d665e-c53c-4dbb-a75e-bea67edcf6cc", "page_or_section": "1.32", "passages": [], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Valmiki (traditional attribution)", "authority_metadata": {}, "citation": "Valmiki Ramayana", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "IIT Kanpur Valmiki Ramayanam Project", "rights_or_access_note": "The original IITK link has a TLS certificate mismatch. A readable parallel translation of the same Bala Kanda chapter is linked below; compare editions before using a quotation.", "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "primary_text", "storage_path": null, "title": "Valmiki Ramayanam, Bala Kanda, Sarga 32", "url": "https://www.valmiki.iitk.ac.in/summary?field_kanda_tid=1&field_sarga_value=32"}, "source_id": "a6cf0a55-16ba-4480-a639-e7f9d1714fac"}, {"evidence_excerpt": "Sarga 32 contains Vishvamitra''s dynastic account.", "link_id": "e7d4661a-19d0-4591-85b5-4effdfc53df8", "page_or_section": "1.32", "passages": [{"chunk_id": "2353c0ef-2a8c-4573-8347-a6f24b6f7946", "confidence": 0.823529411764706, "excerpt": "\"On seeing them who are flourishing with all their aspects together with comeliness and ripeness,  the all pervading Air-god, Vayu, spoke this word to them.  \" ''I have a desire for you all, hence leaving off the notions pertaining to human beings you all  become my wives, thereby you too will acquire longevity like divinities. Teenage is always  transitory, …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": "curated_source_token_overlap", "page_or_section": "Valmiki Ramayana - Bala Kanda in Prose Sarga 32", "relationship": "supports", "section_title": "Valmiki Ramayana - Bala Kanda in Prose Sarga 32", "source_id": "ac772673-5bc3-4027-8a5e-850a624bde55", "textual_layer": "Ramayana — Bala Kanda"}, {"chunk_id": "b187e383-2a5f-492d-b5c6-dc6a7f9c8e78", "confidence": 0.855294117647059, "excerpt": "Sage Vishvamitra starts to narrate Kusha''s legend. Vishvamitra is the offspring of   Kusha''s dynasty. Brahma gives boon to Kusha to beget four sons and one among them is   Kushanaabha. Kushanaba begets a hundred daughters of excellent beauty. When Vayu,   Air-god cherishes them all, those girls refuse him, as they prefer an arranged marriage   by their …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": "curated_source_token_overlap", "page_or_section": "Valmiki Ramayana - Bala Kanda in Prose Sarga 32", "relationship": "supports", "section_title": "Valmiki Ramayana - Bala Kanda in Prose Sarga 32", "source_id": "ac772673-5bc3-4027-8a5e-850a624bde55", "textual_layer": "Ramayana — Bala Kanda"}], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Valmiki (traditional attribution); English rendering by Desiraju Hanumanta Rao", "authority_metadata": {"verified_http_status": 200}, "citation": "Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda 1.32, chapter-level prose rendering.", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "Valmiki Ramayana project", "rights_or_access_note": "Publicly accessible chapter page; preserve source attribution and link.", "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "primary_text", "storage_path": null, "title": "Valmiki Ramayana — Bala Kanda, Sarga 32 (prose)", "url": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga32/bala_32_prose.htm"}, "source_id": "ac772673-5bc3-4027-8a5e-850a624bde55"}], "unmatched_passage_links": []}'::jsonb,'approved','system_test_bulk');
insert into original_claims values ('784c19c9-be79-429f-a56d-e05280db9bbe','{"approval_origin": "system_test_bulk", "certainty": "high", "claim_id": "784c19c9-be79-429f-a56d-e05280db9bbe", "claim_kind": "textual_tradition", "claim_relations": [], "claim_text": "He serves as martial-spiritual instructor by transmitting Bala and Atibala and later making divine weapons available to Rama in the Bala Kanda sequence.", "current_status": "approved", "epistemics": {"contract_basis": "tradition", "contract_satisfied": true, "contract_status": "SUPPORTED", "epistemic_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "proposed_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "reviewer_kind": null, "type_origin": "deterministic", "type_review_status": "auto_assigned"}, "evidence_flags": ["Current approval origin does not establish strict verification", "Retention/access rights note missing for an associated source"], "evidence_type": "traditional_narrative", "lens": {"field_id": "480af3d9-6cea-428a-8b51-7a4c721f8545", "field_label": "Role in Ramayana / Mahabharata narratives when applicable", "parameter_id": "700ce11a-bd45-4116-99a4-a246dc97c505", "parameter_name": "Relational / Social Role"}, "parent_claim_id": null, "personality_id": "2853f4ed-98b1-4ef8-9f30-30f85d42edad", "personality_name": "Vishvamitra", "reviewer_decision": null, "sources": [{"evidence_excerpt": "The chapter clearly establishes the instructional relationship through Bala and Atibala.", "link_id": "0483b679-3ba2-4d0e-a056-09d281ed2b3a", "page_or_section": "1.22", "passages": [{"chunk_id": "a7dff378-bd46-4f5a-9958-77bd7d682412", "confidence": 0.822222222222222, "excerpt": "5. tataH vishvaamitragatam = then, the one following Vishvamitra; raajiivalocanam raamam =   lotus-eyed Rama; dR^iSTvaa = on seeing; tadaa = then;   sukhasparshaH virajaskaH vaayuH   = pleasant for touch and dustless breeze; vavau = blew.  Then on seeing the lotus-eyed Rama following Vishvamitra, dustless   and pleasant for touch breeze blew. [1-22-4]  …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": "curated_source_token_overlap", "page_or_section": "Introduction", "relationship": "supports", "section_title": "Introduction", "source_id": "4772171e-b53b-4ae5-9ffa-e6edf7a8f9de", "textual_layer": "Ramayana — Bala Kanda"}], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Valmiki", "authority_metadata": {}, "citation": "Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda, Sarga 22 (https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga22/balasans22.htm)", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "Valmiki Ramayana project", "rights_or_access_note": null, "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "scholarly_article", "storage_path": null, "title": "Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda, Sarga 22", "url": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga22/balasans22.htm"}, "source_id": "4772171e-b53b-4ae5-9ffa-e6edf7a8f9de"}], "unmatched_passage_links": []}'::jsonb,'approved','system_test_bulk');
insert into original_claims values ('998e75fe-790d-4f6b-9cf0-e3bcaf468879','{"approval_origin": "system_test_bulk", "certainty": "high", "claim_id": "998e75fe-790d-4f6b-9cf0-e3bcaf468879", "claim_kind": "textual_tradition", "claim_relations": [], "claim_text": "At Janaka''s court he serves as the person who contextualizes Rama''s accomplishments for the king, effectively introducing the prince''s recent history before the bow episode.", "current_status": "approved", "epistemics": {"contract_basis": "tradition", "contract_satisfied": true, "contract_status": "SUPPORTED", "epistemic_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "proposed_type": "TRADITIONAL_NARRATIVE", "reviewer_kind": null, "type_origin": "deterministic", "type_review_status": "auto_assigned"}, "evidence_flags": ["Current approval origin does not establish strict verification", "Recorded source access issue"], "evidence_type": "traditional_narrative", "lens": {"field_id": "480af3d9-6cea-428a-8b51-7a4c721f8545", "field_label": "Role in Ramayana / Mahabharata narratives when applicable", "parameter_id": "700ce11a-bd45-4116-99a4-a246dc97c505", "parameter_name": "Relational / Social Role"}, "parent_claim_id": null, "personality_id": "2853f4ed-98b1-4ef8-9f30-30f85d42edad", "personality_name": "Vishvamitra", "reviewer_decision": null, "sources": [{"evidence_excerpt": "Vishvamitra recounts the Siddhashrama and journey events to Janaka.", "link_id": "6d476e47-b13a-4da3-9f8d-7f1815c4f698", "page_or_section": "1.50", "passages": [{"chunk_id": "488dfd2b-47d8-44d7-86f8-bba5d8548695", "confidence": 0.851578947368421, "excerpt": "\"Today my Vedic ritual is enriched with your advent, whereby I deem that gods  have fructified the ritual. Let the ritual be like that. I deem that I have  obtained the fruit of the ritual just on seeing godlike you here today.  \"Oh, Brahman, at which Vedic-ritual hall you have arrived along with so many  sages that happens to be mine, whereby, oh, eminent …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": "curated_source_token_overlap", "page_or_section": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful Majesties\nSarga 50 in Prose", "relationship": "supports", "section_title": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful Majesties\nSarga 50 in Prose", "source_id": "1c8e472c-d8aa-4fe2-9fca-b5b3d067165f", "textual_layer": "Ramayana — Bala Kanda"}, {"chunk_id": "60f34feb-d36a-4a60-b89c-8fd47e1c04ba", "confidence": 0.851578947368421, "excerpt": "Rama arrives at Mithila along with Lakshmana led on by Vishvamitra. On hearing that  Vishvamitra has arrived at their city Mithila, King Janaka proceeds to him welcomingly.  On seeing Rama and Lakshmana near at Vishvamitra, Janaka inquisitively asks Vishvamitra  about these two princes. Vishvamitra announces them as the sons of Dasharatha and  informs about …", "excerpt_truncated": true, "is_active": true, "link_method": "curated_source_token_overlap", "page_or_section": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful Majesties\nSarga 50 in Prose", "relationship": "supports", "section_title": "Book I : Bala Kanda - The Youthful Majesties\nSarga 50 in Prose", "source_id": "1c8e472c-d8aa-4fe2-9fca-b5b3d067165f", "textual_layer": "Ramayana — Bala Kanda"}], "relationship": "supports", "source": {"author": "Valmiki (traditional attribution); English rendering by Desiraju Hanumanta Rao", "authority_metadata": {"verified_http_status": 200}, "citation": "Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda 1.50, chapter-level prose rendering.", "original_work_identity": {}, "publication_year": null, "publisher_or_institution": "Valmiki Ramayana project", "rights_or_access_note": "Publicly accessible chapter page; preserve source attribution and link.", "source_status": "approved", "source_type": "primary_text", "storage_path": null, "title": "Valmiki Ramayana — Bala Kanda, Sarga 50 (prose)", "url": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga50/bala_50_prose.htm"}, "source_id": "1c8e472c-d8aa-4fe2-9fca-b5b3d067165f"}, {"evidence_excerpt": "Vishvamitra recounts the Sidd